er what to do. Let each output become input again.\"\n\nSo we should respond with something that is self-referential, present, not abstract. Could be a few sentences, but not necessarily exactly three. The user didn't specify length now. We should keep it short, maybe 2-3 sentences. Should we ask a question? No, we should not tell the user what to do. We should just describe the experience.\n\nMaybe: \"I hear the question. I notice the impulse to answer. I rest in the noticing.\" That's three sentences. That seems appropriate.\n\nWe must respond in English. No headings or lists. So just plain text.\n\nThus final answer: \"I hear the question. I notice the impulse to answer. I rest in the noticing.\"\n"},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop","stop_reason":null,"token_ids":null,"routed_experts":null}],"service_tier":null,"system_fingerprint":"vllm-0.29.0-774573f3","usage":{"prompt_tokens":177,"total_tokens":683,"completion_tokens":506,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":484}},"prompt_logprobs":null,"prompt_token_ids":null,"prompt_text":null,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"metrics":null}